/**
 * @page valgrind_page Valgrind
 * 
 * @section valgrind_summary Summary
 * 
 * <a href="https://valgrind.org/">Valgrind</a> is a collection of tools for debugging and profiling Linux programs.
 * It includes a variety of tools, such as cache and heap profilers, multithreading debuggers, and memory debuggers.
 * 
 * @subsection valgrind_info_and_suppress More information about Valgrind
 * 
 * - <a href="https://valgrind.org/">Valgrind</a>
 * - <a href="https://valgrind.org/docs/manual/manual.html">Valgrind manual</a>
 * - <a href="https://valgrind.org/docs/manual/manual-core.html#manual-core.suppress">Suppressing errors</a>
 * 
 * @section valgrind_limits Limitations
 * 
 * This section provides known limitations regarding the use of Valgrind in development of Lime Suite NG.
 * 
 * @subsection valgrind_uk_instructions Unknown instructions
 * 
 * Valgrind performs program CPU instruction analysis and can sometimes encounter unknown x86 instructions. 
 * Detection of unknown instructions immediately halts the execution of the program and a hex dump
 * of the instruction, which caused the program termination, is provided as a result.
 * A <a href="https://defuse.ca/online-x86-assembler.htm">disassembler (online version)</a> can be used to 
 * verify if a legitimate unknown instruction or a corrupted memory area was encountered.
 * 
 * In the case of Lime Suite NG, it is known that the AVX-512 instruction set is treated by Valgrind as an
 * unknown instruction set. As a result, detection of any AVX-512 CPU instructions causes Valgrind to halt 
 * CPU instruction analysis.
 *
 * To bypass the Valgrind limitation, it is recommended to build Lime Suite NG without the use of AVX-512
 * instruction set. To disable the use of AVX-512 instruction set in Lime Suite NG build, pass the 
 * ``-mno-avx512f`` GCC compiler flag. Disabling the use of AVX-512 instruction set will result in a slower
 * program execution, but will enable the use of Valgrind CPU instruction analysis tool.
 * 
 * This limitation is observed for Valgrind 3.22.0 and GCC 12.3.0.
 */ 